      <div type="editorial-notes">
        <head>Transcription notes</head>
        <note xml:id="W-3.6-note-1" n="1" type="observation" target="#W-3.6-l1" resp="#W-3.6-encoder">The printed poem heading is present above this witness text and is transcribed separately in heading metadata.</note>
        <note xml:id="W-3.6-note-2" n="2" type="observation" target="#W-3.6-l2" resp="#W-3.6-reviewer">The two-line opening capital displaces verse 2 farther right than the ordinary inset. An additional horizontal space of three characters approximates this observed layout.</note>
        <note xml:id="W-3.6-note-46" n="46" type="uncertainty" target="#W-3.6-l46" resp="#W-3.6-reviewer">The source clearly prints spumifer before arva, without an additional a. A tiny intervening mark resembles a full stop but cannot securely be separated from the adjacent type or surface; the possible punctuation is locally marked unclear.</note>
      </div>
